  "culture": {
    "title": "Athens in 432 BC",
    "md": "The story you are about to read is set in the summer of 432 BC. Athens is at the height of its power: the Parthenon has just been finished, Pericles leads the assembly, the fleet rules the Aegean, and the city's potters export their red-figure vases from Spain to the Black Sea. In the Agora, the open square at the foot of the Acropolis, citizens shop, argue, vote and gossip. War with Sparta is one year away. Ariston, a potter with a workshop in the Kerameikos, his wife Chrysis, their children Lysis and Elpis, old Kleinias, the slave Syros and the dog Labros are made up; everything around them is as the excavations and the texts describe it.",
    "image": "polis"
  },
